; scalygpu - GPU (Metal) device residency for scaly.tensor tapes.
;
; Package root. A program that wants its tape on the GPU declares this
; package and holds a GpuTape (use scalygpu.gputape.GpuTape) - device
; placement is visible at the type level, never hidden. There is NO
; silent CPU fallback: attaching without a Metal device is a loud,
; fatal error; the explicit CPU path is the bare Tape. Programs that
; want a portable SKIP check GpuTape.available() first.
;
; The scaly_mgpu_* extern declarations live in this package's sources,
; so they are compiled ONLY into GPU programs - libscaly.a stays free
; of them (an archive member referencing scaly_mgpu_* would break
; every non-macOS link). The Obj-C shim stays out of the archive too:
; tools/mgpu.sh compiles packages/scaly/0.1.1/scaly/tensor/mgpu.m and
; programs link the object plus -framework Metal -framework
; MetalPerformanceShaders -framework Foundation explicitly.

package scaly 0.1.0

define scalygpu
{
    module gputape
}
